<% content_for :title, "Spike or Stay: will this trend last?" %>
<% content_for :description, ApplicationHelper::DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION %>
<%= render "shared/nav" %>

<main>
  <%# ---------- Hero ---------- %>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <span class="badge"><span class="badge-dot"></span>Backtested on <%= TrendModel.instance.trained_on["n"] %> past trends · zero lookahead</span>
        <h1>Get an early read on whether a trend will <em>stay</em>.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Some products blow up overnight and are forgotten a month later (remember fidget spinners?).
          Others keep selling for years. This tool, made for Shopify store owners, tells you which is which.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <%= link_to "Open the dashboard", dashboard_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
          <%= link_to "See how it works", methodology_path, class: "btn btn-outline btn-lg" %>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">Made to support Shopify businesses · Free demo with sample products, no sign-up needed</p>
      </div>

      <%# Illustration of a real replay result (Air fryer, Dec 31 2017): label, confidence and onset are real. %>
      <div class="hero-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="float-chip chip-top"><span class="chip-icon up">↑</span><div><strong>5.8× usual level</strong><span>over the first 6 weeks</span></div></div>
        <div class="mock-card">
          <div class="mock-head">
            <div><span class="mock-kicker">Kitchen · Air fryer</span><strong>5.8qt Basket Air Fryer</strong></div>
            <span class="label tone-success"><span class="label-dot"></span>Likely sustained · 67%</span>
          </div>
          <svg class="mock-chart" viewBox="0 0 320 120" preserveAspectRatio="none">
            <defs><linearGradient id="hero-fill" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#059669" stop-opacity="0.25"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#059669" stop-opacity="0"/></linearGradient></defs>
            <line x1="0" x2="320" y1="72" y2="72" class="mock-ref"/>
            <rect x="244" y="6" width="44" height="108" class="mock-window"/>
            <polygon fill="url(#hero-fill)" points="0,120 0,104 20,103 40,101 60,99 80,100 100,96 120,92 140,95 160,90 180,93 200,91 220,88 236,80 244,70 252,52 260,14 268,40 276,36 284,28 292,46 300,50 320,56 320,120"/>
            <polyline class="mock-line" points="0,104 20,103 40,101 60,99 80,100 100,96 120,92 140,95 160,90 180,93 200,91 220,88 236,80 244,70 252,52 260,14 268,40 276,36 284,28 292,46 300,50 320,56"/>
          </svg>
          <div class="mock-foot"><span><i class="key key-dash"></i>Surge bar</span><span><i class="key key-window"></i>6 weeks the model reads</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="float-chip chip-bottom"><span class="chip-icon">◷</span><div><strong>Onset · Nov 6, 2017</strong><span>Replay, no data after Dec 31</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ---------- Stat strip (all real) ---------- %>
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="stat-strip">
      <div><strong><%= TrendModel.instance.trained_on["n"] %></strong><span>past trends backtested</span></div>
      <div><strong><%= BacktestStats.percent(:a, :logreg).delete_suffix("%") %><em>%</em></strong><span>leave-one-out accuracy (95% CI <%= BacktestStats.interval(:a, :logreg) %>)</span></div>
      <div><strong>6<em> wks</em></strong><span>of data before each call</span></div>
      <div><strong>0</strong><span>weeks of lookahead, enforced by tests</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ---------- How it works ---------- %>
  <section class="section" id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2>From your catalog to a call, in three steps</h2>
        <p>No sales data needed. Just your products and what the world is reading about them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><span class="step-num">1</span><h3>Match products to interest</h3><p>Each product's type (or title) is matched to a Wikipedia article, with a sanity check and one-click fixes when the match is wrong.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="step-num">2</span><h3>Spot an abrupt surge</h3><p>A surge starts when weekly views beat 3× their usual level and 2,000 views, two weeks in a row. One-day news blips don't count.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="step-num">3</span><h3>Call it from six weeks</h3><p>A logistic regression reads only the first six weeks after the surge and estimates the chance it's still going strong half a year later.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ---------- Feature rows ---------- %>
  <section class="section section-tight">
    <div class="wrap feature">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Your whole catalog</p>
        <h2>Every product's trend, at a glance</h2>
        <p>One card per product, with a 26-week sparkline, a clear label and a plain-English reason. Filter to just the surges in one click.</p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><strong>Grouped automatically</strong>: twelve snowboards that share an article are one card</li>
          <li><strong>Honest labels</strong>: "Not enough data" and "Not mapped" instead of a guess</li>
          <li><strong>Live from Shopify</strong>: active products only, via the Admin API</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="mini-grid">
          <div class="mini-card"><span class="label tone-success"><span class="label-dot"></span>Likely sustained</span><strong>Air fryer</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 100 24" preserveAspectRatio="none"><polyline class="spark-success" points="0,20 20,19 40,18 55,15 65,10 72,3 80,8 90,6 100,9"/></svg></div>
          <div class="mini-card"><span class="label tone-warning"><span class="label-dot"></span>Likely spike</span><strong>Fidget spinner</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 100 24" preserveAspectRatio="none"><polyline class="spark-warning" points="0,21 20,20 35,16 45,6 52,2 60,9 72,15 85,18 100,20"/></svg></div>
          <div class="mini-card"><span class="label tone-caution"><span class="label-dot"></span>Too early to tell</span><strong>Dubai chocolate</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 100 24" preserveAspectRatio="none"><polyline class="spark-caution" points="0,21 30,20 60,19 72,14 82,7 90,5 100,6"/></svg></div>
          <div class="mini-card"><span class="label tone-neutral"><span class="label-dot"></span>No surge</span><strong>Matcha</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 100 24" preserveAspectRatio="none"><polyline class="spark-neutral" points="0,12 15,13 30,11 45,12 60,10 75,12 90,11 100,12"/></svg></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap feature feature-flip">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Explainable by design</p>
        <h2>Know why, not just what</h2>
        <p>Open any product to see two years of interest, the surge bar it cleared, and how each early signal pushed the model toward "sustained" or "spike".</p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><strong>Interactive chart</strong> with the onset and the six weeks the model read</li>
          <li><strong>Per-feature contributions</strong> that add up to the shown probability</li>
          <li><strong>Plain-language reasons</strong>: "Interest 5.8× its usual level, holding steady"</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="explain-mock">
          <strong>How the model decided</strong>
          <div class="em-row"><span>Peak sharpness</span><div class="em-bar"><i class="pos" style="width:46%"></i></div><b>+0.77</b></div>
          <div class="em-row"><span>Volatility</span><div class="em-bar"><i class="pos" style="width:19%"></i></div><b>+0.31</b></div>
          <div class="em-row"><span>Acceleration</span><div class="em-bar"><i class="neg" style="width:5%"></i></div><b>−0.07</b></div>
          <div class="em-row"><span>Growth</span><div class="em-bar"><i class="neg" style="width:3%"></i></div><b>−0.04</b></div>
          <p>Starting point −0.25, plus these pushes → <strong>67%</strong> chance of sustained.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap feature" id="replays">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Replay mode</p>
        <h2>Rewind to any week since 2016</h2>
        <p>See exactly what the app would have said on a past date, using only the data that existed then. A good way to sanity-check it against trends you remember.</p>
        <div class="replay-links">
          <%= link_to dashboard_path(as_of: "2017-06-12"), class: "replay-card" do %>
            <span class="label tone-warning"><span class="label-dot"></span>Likely spike</span><strong>Fidget spinners</strong><span>June 12, 2017 ›</span>
          <% end %>
          <%= link_to dashboard_path(as_of: "2017-12-31"), class: "replay-card" do %>
            <span class="label tone-success"><span class="label-dot"></span>Likely sustained</span><strong>Air fryers</strong><span>December 31, 2017 ›</span>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <p class="fineprint">These trends were in the training data, so replays demo the pipeline rather than prove accuracy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="timeline-mock">
          <div class="tl-track"><span style="left:8%"></span><span style="left:30%"></span><span class="is-on" style="left:52%"></span><span style="left:78%"></span></div>
          <div class="tl-labels"><span>2016</span><span>2017</span><span>2018</span><span>2020</span></div>
          <p><strong>as_of = 2017-12-31</strong><br>Only weeks ending on or before Dec 24, 2017 are used.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ---------- Honest by design (navy band) ---------- %>
  <section class="trust">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-intro section-intro-dark">
        <p class="eyebrow">Honest by design</p>
        <h2>Built like a study, not a sales pitch</h2>
        <p>The rules were written down before the results existed, and every number comes with its sample size.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trust-grid">
        <div><h3>Pre-registered</h3><p>Thresholds, features and analyses were committed before any model ran. Two later changes are logged with reasons.</p></div>
        <div><h3>No lookahead</h3><p>Features read only six weeks of data, and tests feed in fake future data to prove it changes nothing.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Uncertainty shown</h3><p>Accuracy comes with a 95% confidence interval and n = <%= TrendModel.instance.trained_on["n"] %>. Small sample, said plainly.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="trust-link"><%= link_to "Read the full methodology ›", methodology_path %></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ---------- FAQ ---------- %>
  <section class="section section-soft" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Questions, answered</p>
        <h2>What people ask first</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>Why Wikipedia pageviews?</summary><p>They're free, public, daily and go back to 2015, so the model can be backtested on real past trends. They measure interest, not sales: readers aren't buyers, and brand articles dilute product interest. That's listed as a limitation.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What counts as a "surge"?</summary><p>Weekly views above 3× the median of the previous 26 weeks and at least 2,000 views, for two weeks in a row. Slow, gradual growth never triggers this, so those products show "No surge detected".</p></details>
        <details><summary>How accurate is it?</summary><p>On <%= TrendModel.instance.trained_on["n"] %> past trends, <%= BacktestStats.percent(:a, :logreg) %> leave-one-out accuracy (95% CI <%= BacktestStats.interval(:a, :logreg) %>), versus <%= BacktestStats.percent(:a, :naive) %> for a simple "still rising in week 6" rule. That's a promising signal, but the gap is within noise at this sample size.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does it use my sales data?</summary><p>Not yet. It reads only product titles, types and tags. Tying labels to order data is the top next step.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What if a product maps to the wrong article?</summary><p>Every card has a "Fix mapping" form: point the product at the right article, or mark it "Don't track". Fixes apply to every product with the same search term.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ---------- CTA ---------- %>
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="cta">
      <h2>See what's surging in your catalog</h2>
      <p>Connect a Shopify dev store, or explore the demo with sample products.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <%= link_to "Open the dashboard", dashboard_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
        <%= link_to "Try a replay", dashboard_path(as_of: "2017-12-31"), class: "btn btn-ghost btn-lg" %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<%= render "shared/footer" %>
